        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Kinematic transformations {s}-{b}",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Taking small angle approximations",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\Rightarrow$",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Hence, we obtain the sought transformation:",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Kinematic transformations {s}-{b}",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "To relate the accelerations",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "where",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/801af0349b0aff4e5515bf3b2c63f0c9deadac39ad5098b2ffad6848b59a73e4.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Taking small angle approximations and considering only linear terms",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/1fd2d9d82e57f6511e1a691f853d20cf865d2a7ac79950e786d5ea6602ff873a.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Which is consistent with",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Kinematic transformations {s}-{b}",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Velocities:",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Accelerations:",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/37363954bf1975efe1b97c187f32cb979b54980d9ac1616ee5d3971edd7c8b63.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Generalised Positions:",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Now we can transform the Cummins Equation to {b}.",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "RB seakeeping Eq. of motion in {s}",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Using the body-fixed perturbation coordinates we have",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "linear",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Non-linear",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/56fc4151c8dd2b9e3749e372e5a60009e37fb48dba964cf019e95c4b217dda88.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "RB seakeeping Eq. of motion in {s}",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "We can think the linear-seakeeping equations of motion",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "as obtained from the body-fixed perturbation equations considering",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/f9b09c3ce1132e5d96b3a8056a4424f98ab9db9621b13fce7724a5f336ff45dc.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "NOTE: In the literature, it is commonly said that the seakeeping eq of motion is formulated in {s}, but this would imply that the inertias are time varying.",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "In our derivation, we formulate them in body-fixed coordinated and then ignore the nonlinear terms; this way, the inertias are constant because we are in body-fixed coordinates.",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Cummins Equation in {b}",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/4be09e444f53f961847ccb1a0e7219e7275605b4fba8f7dac36ed4badc855aa0.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\Updownarrow$",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/f9b09c3ce1132e5d96b3a8056a4424f98ab9db9621b13fce7724a5f336ff45dc.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This model describes deviations from the equilibrium state in {b} within a linear framework and small angles.",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Cummins Equation in {b}",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Expressed in terms of absolute (instead of incremental) variables:",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "NOTE: This equation valid provided the manoeuvring is very slow—because of the seakeeping assumptions under which the Cummins eq. was derived.",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Summary",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- The problem of manoeuvring in a seaway is still an open problem in ship theory."
        ],
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- A step towards a unified model for manoeuvring in a sea way consists of expressing Cummins Equation in {b}."
        ],
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- This is still a seakeeping model, which assumes a state of equilibrium from which the vessel is disturbed; and therefore, it may be use it for slow manoeuvring."
        ],
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- For slow manoeuvring, we can add Lift-Drag effects as a first approximation."
        ],
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 18
    },
